TJR wrote on Sat, 27 Nov 2010 05:42:22 -0800 (PST):
> But then the tedium kicked in: I was ready to ascend, except that I
> had absolutely no way to harm Rodney. This weaponless, wishless, poly-
> foo-less pacifist searched the entire dungeons (except the sanctum and
> perhaps Ludios) but never found a ring of conflict

Seems a bit silly to complain about the RNG when you are attempting an 
especially hard multi-conduct ascension in which you've forsworn all the 
main methods the game gives the player to obtain items not otherwise 
generated: wishing, polypiling, death drops.

NEVERTHELESS,

Spell of confuse monster, combined with appropriate tame (or not) 
monsters would have worked.  Lacking the spell, you could have tamed an 
umber hulk, confused it with a mirror, and waited for it to confuse other 
monsters.

> The purple worm ate all the Valley
> wraith, then died. 

This was entirely predictable.  You'd probably have done better to level 
yourself up first to make sure you could tame an archon if needed.

> After alchemy had left me with a very expensive
> stack of booze but no gain level,

Farm monster starting inventories (perhaps in a throne room) for more 
potions.


